+# Standalone admission fix publication and prototype restoration
+
+Commit the tested standalone repair before restoring the parked prototypes. This keeps the native commit equal to the compiled/tested two-file source image. Restoring first would force a partial-index commit of bodies different from the working tree and invalidate the simple source/epoch checks. This plan performs no transitions and records no acceptance.
+
+## Required evidence
+
+The new comparison runner must explicitly authorize the artifact-only successor from frozen `e2839ec561c1` to signed checkpoint `b7583cb3a5908bc26deaf5bedab242c4c8fd8633`, preserving the original experiment and compiled candidate body/binary/application metadata pins. Require complete raw lifecycle, no execution/preservation errors, owned process/profile cleanup, exact original adoption, and independent raw assessment. The original A result is 57 PASS/47 FAIL; the candidate must have all 104 A assertions PASS, all 16 held B signatures unchanged (including observed values/messages, not merely FAIL), and all 446 existing assertions plus six reftests unchanged. Bind every mutation callback's terminal assertion. Require the sign observer's full original/candidate snapshots to match under its explicit comparison contract; any drift needs adjudication before acceptance. Preserve separately obtained zoom evidence and resolve any newly observed candidate regression rather than attributing it to the known baseline defect. No browser comparison has been performed by this plan.
+
+The build must remain the successful `head-candidate-build-2` image with the exact HEAD-proposal-v3 source hashes. Do not give native-refinement, security, or canonical coverage credit. Pending B scheduling, unresolved self-font policy, and the independent zoom normalization lead are excluded from this fix.
+
+## Publication order
+
+1. Finish and independently review the candidate browser comparisons while native sources remain in the standalone role. Freeze their raw evidence and acceptance decision; do not restore prototype sources yet.
+2. Install only `testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-properties-values-api/registered-numeric-selected-dependencies.html` from the sealed fixture-v3 candidate capture. Require absence in HEAD and on disk (including no symlink), authenticate the fixture manifest, `A-WPT.patch`, tested capsule copy, and installed bytes. Expected page SHA-256 is `8d3b7ef01fae8d1b4efe03f7fb30821bac1bb72ac93c18c7d20275c5ef06926a`. Record exclusive creation, regular-file identity, mode, parent ownership, before/after epoch and raw/semantic index preservation. Add its hash and identity to the current epoch without changing the other source, binary, untracked companion or nested-index pins. The B research page and metadata are excluded. The candidate experiment already executes this exact page, so copying unchanged bytes does not need a native rebuild; retain the existing WPT lint/manifest evidence and verify installed identity against the tested capture.
+3. Seal the comparison, installation receipt, review, acceptance and exact-three-path packaging artifacts. Commit this tooling/documentation/evidence in a preceding signed research commit. Record the artifact-only HEAD successor explicitly; this is not a new browser run. Existing earlier source-proposal and tools commits remain ancestors.
+4. Make one signed standalone fix commit with exactly `servo/components/style/custom_properties.rs`, `servo/components/style/properties/cascade.rs`, and the A WPT path. Use the existing guarded signing helper with an explicit three-path selection and current epoch. The two native hashes are `83a9bcbe4768f609679d46d6bb81ebd0329ad33503824286b52efe4c3309a0d7` and `1c3df7c608722ca9d16de7f04fd8d6fbc2ea7b509443ae591a9db69b014e3c0e`. Verify the commit's parent, signature, exact diff paths, modes and resulting blob hashes, and unchanged working/native/binary bodies. The expected tracked native dirty set becomes empty. Retain all 50 parked prototype bodies and all untracked companion pins. No collector, pending-test overlay, artifact, metadata or B-test path belongs in this commit.
+5. Only after that verified receipt, update the fix ledgers in a separate administrative checkpoint. Proposed next identifier is fix 139; accepted/committed totals advance 137→138 and tracked records 138→139, with held fix 120 still excluded. Group this root-cause family under Attributes and custom properties (18→19). Do not count the 47 repaired assertions or the pending 76-case B lead as separate fixes. Preserve signing/history arrays and prior entries. Bind the preceding research commit, native commit, exact acceptance/raw evidence and tested hashes in the new entry. Update CURRENT-COMMITS, GROUPS, BUGFIX-COMMITS, readout README and PLAN consistently; canonical counts remain unchanged. A passing candidate alone does not justify `COMMITTED_NATIVE_WPT`; require the signed three-path receipt as well.
+
+## Restoration after publication
+
+Prepare a small immutable successor of the existing transition tool after the native commit is known. Merely rebinding `paired_head` is insufficient: v4 assumes the two HEAD blobs are old `head_original`, the two native files are dirty, the transition is unaccepted, and the saved WPT epoch equals the current epoch. Those assumptions cease to hold after publication. Authenticate the exact tested epoch→research commits→three-path fix→ledger-checkpoint chain, without treating that chain as fresh runtime validation. Extend the exact two-ledger v8→v14→v15→v16 chain through the new administrative checkpoint; leave the other 138 recovery pins unchanged.
+
+For restoration, authorize the new HEAD's two native blobs as the tested candidate, the added A WPT as immutable committed content, and the remaining 48 original native blobs unchanged. Preserve the original RESTORATION-PLAN and original captures as historical inputs. Acquire current file identities from the verified ownership/epoch rather than trusting a stale owner hash. Expected pre-restoration tracked native dirt is empty. Authenticate all 50 parked bodies, then install the full prototype image with the sealed live-v3 two-file overlay, preserving the new A WPT and the six untouched collector files. Verify the complete destination image and derive the dirty set against the new HEAD; do not overwrite HEAD's accepted fix with the old standalone original. Mark the restored prototype role uncompiled and uncertified, retaining a separate pointer to the accepted standalone fix.
+
+Only then apply the separately gated pending-GTest overlay, rebind its validator to the new HEAD with the same source contracts, build, and run all 22 tests in four suites (34 static source calls). Its outcome validates pending integration, not the already accepted standalone repair or B scheduling as a whole. Preserve all source/index/nested/rollback guards and reuse the existing build directory.
+
+## Scope of inspection
+
+Read-only inspection of the sealed source transition, signing helper, epoch verifier, fixture and current ledger snapshots informed this plan. No Git/source/epoch/index/build/browser mutation or new runtime validation occurred. Inputs are pinned in INPUTS.json. Final source/test/acceptance packages must be rebound to whatever exact successor HEAD the parent selects for execution.
